## **Github Amdonition** {underline}`Markdown` {style}`Flavor <color=#1a7f37 mark=#cde7ff>`

Nootropy support Github Markdown style admonition:

```md
> [!NOTE] 
> 💡Use Note for general context, links to related docs, or anything informational. 
```

renders as =>

> [!NOTE] 
> 💡Use Note for general context, links to related docs, or anything informational. 

```md
> [!TIP] 
> ✅ Use Tip for shortcuts, optimizations, or the > "you probably also want…" hint.
```
renders as =>

> [!TIP] 
> ✅ Use Tip for shortcuts, optimizations, or the > "you probably also want…" hint. 

> [!IMPORTANT]  📌 **A malform gfm admonition is considered as blockquote** Use Important when the reader needs to know this before they act on the rest of the doc.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 📌 **A wellform gfm admonition** Use Important when the reader needs to know this before they act on the rest of the doc.

With markdown only 0 or 1 space is allowed after the admonition name ex: `> [!WARNING]` or `> [!WARNING] `

This block 
```md
> [!WARNING] 
⚠️ Use Warning for things that will surprise people: breaking changes, side effects, footguns. 
```
render as: 

> [!WARNING] 
⚠️ Use Warning for things that will surprise people: breaking changes, side effects, footguns.
**Note**: This is a **Malform GFM warning** so the renderer will see it as ambiguous/opaque

 

> [!CAUTION] 
> 🛑 Use Caution for the dangerous stuff. Data loss, irreversible operations, security gotchas.

